<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      node_radio_device — the control-plane SOURCE OF TRUTH for a Meshtastic LoRa RADIO an
      operator ATTACHES to a specific mesh node, so the meshbridge optional service (the
      mesh<->Matrix bridge, built in parallel) can reach the LoRa mesh THROUGH that node.
      CLONES the node-storage (085) pool idioms verbatim — one table (a radio has no
      per-radio sub-assignments the way a pool has service placements):

        node_radio_device — a radio attachment PINNED to one node (FK -> device_registry).
                            Identity is the node + a stable bridge-facing radio_id; the row
                            carries the TRANSPORT the node reaches the radio over:
                              serial — a USB-serial Meshtastic device on THAT node
                                       (serial_path, e.g. /dev/ttyUSB0);
                              tcp    — a LoRa-WiFi radio the node dials over TCP
                                       (host + port, Meshtastic TCP API port 4403);
                              mqtt   — a WAN-linked / LoRaWAN-gateway-style mesh reached via
                                       a Meshtastic MQTT broker (host + port [1883] +
                                       topic_root + channel_name, optional gateway_node_id
                                       for downlink attribution) — NOT a locally attached
                                       radio.
                            Per-node + per-domain; CAS active->detached (never DELETE =
                            audit); generation + propagation_state drive the on-node
                            reconcile ACK exactly like 085's pools.

      ── Portable DDL (mirrors 085-node-storage.xml + the 270 new-table id DEFAULT) ────
      id is a varchar(36) UUID string with the org-wide DB-generated DEFAULT
      ((gen_random_uuid())::text, the changelog-200 idiom): the INSERT omits id and reads it
      back via RETURNING id. timestamptz -> the portable 'timestamp with time zone' generic
      type, defaultValueComputed="now()". One changeSet per CHECK / partial-unique / FK /
      index / GRANT (independent redeploy + rollback). PG-gated partial-unique + indexes +
      GRANT via a dbms=postgresql precondition (onFail/onError=MARK_RAN) — the non-PG path
      enforces the at-most-one-active invariant with the service findActive-before-insert
      guard, exactly like 085. NEVER a DELETE grant — detach is a CAS UPDATE.

      ── DOMAIN stamped from the node's RESIDENCY (not the caller) [FIX-NODEFAULT] ─────
      The table carries a per-row `domain` tenant discriminator for the ADMIN read view,
      but it is NEVER caller-supplied: the service resolves the node FIRST and stamps the
      radio domain from device_registry.domain (the node's residency), exactly as 085's
      attachPool() stamps pool.domain from the device's residency.

      ── OWNERSHIP gating is in the SERVICE, not the schema (the 085 divergence kept) ──
      Radios are ADMIN-CAPABLE (not superadmin-only) but OWNERSHIP-gated: an ADMIN may act
      ONLY on own-domain ADMIN-owned nodes; any SUPERADMIN-owned node is SUPERADMIN-only;
      SUPERADMIN is unrestricted. That ALLOW/DENY matrix is enforced in the service layer
      reading device_registry.owner_type + PrincipalDomain residency — the schema only
      records owner_type via the FK'd device row, exactly like 085.

      ── TRANSPORT shape (per-transport column matrix, CHECK-backstopped) ──────────────
      transport IN ('serial','tcp','mqtt'). serial -> serial_path required, host/port/
      topic_root/channel_name/gateway_node_id absent; tcp -> host+port required,
      serial_path/topic_root/channel_name/gateway_node_id absent; mqtt -> host+port+
      topic_root+channel_name required, gateway_node_id optional, serial_path absent. The
      service rejects a mixed shape (422) BEFORE any write; the ck_node_radio_device_shape
      CHECK is the DB backstop, mirroring how 085 pairs service guards with CHECKs.

      ── propagation_state + generation (reconcile ACK + rollback) ─────────────────────
      Same CHECK vocabulary as 085 (pending/applied/failed/degraded) so the UI can show
      the on-node meshbridge reconcile ACK, plus a monotonic `generation` bumped on every
      mutate that the per-node signed export's monotonic-generation rollback guard reads
      (the export reproduces NodeStorageExportService.exportNode exactly).

      ── SHIPS INERT (opt-in / attach-by-command) ──────────────────────────────────────
      The table is created EMPTY. With zero radio rows the platform behaves EXACTLY as
      today (the meshbridge optional service has nothing to reconcile). A node radio is an
      OPTIONAL attachment the operator opts into per node.

      ── Numbering: 300 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Current max band on main is 290/291 (account localparts). 300 is the NEXT FREE band.
      Appended LAST at the include site in db.changelog-master.xml, after the 291 include.
      Independent of every other changeSet (a net-new table).
    -->

    <!-- ════════════════════════ node_radio_device ════════════════════════════════ -->

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>node_radio_device — a Meshtastic LoRa radio attachment PINNED to ONE mesh
                 node (FK -> device_registry): USB-serial on the node, a LoRa-WiFi radio
                 dialled over TCP, or a WAN mesh reached via a Meshtastic MQTT broker.
                 domain is stamped from the node's RESIDENCY by the service
                 [FIX-NODEFAULT], never the caller.</comment>
        <createTable tableName="node_radio_device">
            <column name="id" type="varchar(36)" defaultValueComputed="(gen_random_uuid())::text">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- The node this radio is attached to / reachable from. A radio is NODE-PINNED:
                 the on-node meshbridge reconcile agent bridges exactly the radios pinned to
                 ITS node. -->
            <column name="device_id" type="varchar(36)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- HOW the node reaches the radio: 'serial' (USB-serial device path on the
                 node) | 'tcp' (LoRa-WiFi radio, Meshtastic TCP API, default port 4403)
                 | 'mqtt' (WAN/LoRaWAN-gateway mesh via a Meshtastic MQTT broker, JSON
                 integration, default port 1883). -->
            <column name="transport" type="varchar(16)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- serial transport ONLY: the node-local serial device path
                 (e.g. /dev/ttyUSB0, /dev/serial/by-id/...). NULL for tcp/mqtt. -->
            <column name="serial_path" type="varchar(255)"/>
            <!-- tcp + mqtt transports ONLY: the radio's / broker's hostname or IPv4. NULL
                 for serial. -->
            <column name="host" type="varchar(253)"/>
            <!-- tcp + mqtt transports ONLY: the TCP port (Meshtastic API 4403 / MQTT 1883).
                 NULL for serial. -->
            <column name="port" type="int"/>
            <!-- mqtt transport ONLY: the broker topic root the mesh publishes under
                 (e.g. msh/US). NULL for serial/tcp. -->
            <column name="topic_root" type="varchar(64)"/>
            <!-- mqtt transport ONLY: the Meshtastic channel name the JSON integration
                 subscribes on. NULL for serial/tcp. -->
            <column name="channel_name" type="varchar(32)"/>
            <!-- mqtt transport ONLY (optional): the mesh GATEWAY node id used for downlink
                 attribution (Meshtastic !hex8 node id). NULL elsewhere. -->
            <column name="gateway_node_id" type="varchar(16)"/>
            <!-- The stable bridge-facing radio identity the meshbridge keys its channel map
                 on; UNIQUE per node while active (re-attaching the same radio_id on the
                 same node is idempotent). -->
            <column name="radio_id" type="varchar(64)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- The Meshtastic mesh channel index (0..7) the bridge binds this radio on. -->
            <column name="mesh_channel" type="int" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="state" type="varchar(16)" defaultValue="active">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- home/tenant discriminator for the ADMIN read view — stamped from the node's
                 residency by the service (NO default residency is reachable). -->
            <column name="domain" type="varchar(64)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- the on-node meshbridge reconcile ACK outcome the UI surfaces. -->
            <column name="propagation_state" type="varchar(16)" defaultValue="pending">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <!-- monotonic generation bumped on every mutate; the per-node signed export
                 carries max(generation) so a node rejects a rolled-back payload. -->
            <column name="generation" type="bigint" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_by" type="varchar(400)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="timestamp with time zone" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="detached_at" type="timestamp with time zone"/>
            <column name="detached_by" type="varchar(400)"/>
        </createTable>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-transport-check" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>CHECK: transport is serial (USB-serial on the node), tcp (LoRa-WiFi radio,
                 Meshtastic TCP API) or mqtt (WAN mesh via a Meshtastic MQTT broker).</comment>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE node_radio_device
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_transport
                CHECK (transport IN ('serial', 'tcp', 'mqtt'))
        </sql>
        <rollback>ALTER TABLE node_radio_device DROP CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_transport</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-shape-check" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>CHECK: the per-transport column matrix — serial rows carry ONLY serial_path;
                 tcp rows carry ONLY host+port; mqtt rows carry host+port+topic_root+
                 channel_name (gateway_node_id optional). The DB backstop to the service's
                 mixed-shape reject (422), like 085's service-guard + CHECK pairing.</comment>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE node_radio_device
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_shape
                CHECK (
                    (transport = 'serial' AND serial_path IS NOT NULL AND host IS NULL
                        AND port IS NULL AND topic_root IS NULL AND channel_name IS NULL
                        AND gateway_node_id IS NULL)
                 OR (transport = 'tcp' AND serial_path IS NULL AND host IS NOT NULL
                        AND port IS NOT NULL AND topic_root IS NULL AND channel_name IS NULL
                        AND gateway_node_id IS NULL)
                 OR (transport = 'mqtt' AND serial_path IS NULL AND host IS NOT NULL
                        AND port IS NOT NULL AND topic_root IS NOT NULL
                        AND channel_name IS NOT NULL)
                )
        </sql>
        <rollback>ALTER TABLE node_radio_device DROP CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_shape</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-state-check" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>CHECK: state is active (bridged) or detached (CAS audit, never DELETEd
                 while history matters).</comment>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE node_radio_device
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_state
                CHECK (state IN ('active', 'detached'))
        </sql>
        <rollback>ALTER TABLE node_radio_device DROP CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_state</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-propagation-check" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>CHECK: propagation_state is one of the four push-with-ack outcomes
                 (same vocabulary as 085's node_storage_pool).</comment>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE node_radio_device
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_propagation
                CHECK (propagation_state IN ('pending', 'applied', 'failed', 'degraded'))
        </sql>
        <rollback>ALTER TABLE node_radio_device DROP CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_propagation</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-mesh-channel-check" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>CHECK: the Meshtastic mesh channel index is 0..7 (the radio's 8 channel
                 slots).</comment>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE node_radio_device
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_mesh_channel
                CHECK (mesh_channel BETWEEN 0 AND 7)
        </sql>
        <rollback>ALTER TABLE node_radio_device DROP CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_mesh_channel</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-port-check" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>CHECK: when present, port is a real TCP port (1..65535).</comment>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE node_radio_device
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_port
                CHECK (port IS NULL OR port BETWEEN 1 AND 65535)
        </sql>
        <rollback>ALTER TABLE node_radio_device DROP CONSTRAINT ck_node_radio_device_port</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-device-fk" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>FK: a radio's device_id references a real device_registry row (the node it
                 is attached to). The radio's residency + owner_type are READ THROUGH this FK
                 (the service stamps domain from device.domain, gates on device.owner_type).</comment>
        <addForeignKeyConstraint
                constraintName="fk_node_radio_device_device"
                baseTableName="node_radio_device" baseColumnNames="device_id"
                referencedTableName="device_registry" referencedColumnNames="id"/>
        <rollback>
            <dropForeignKeyConstraint baseTableName="node_radio_device"
                                      constraintName="fk_node_radio_device_device"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
      The partial UNIQUE below is PARTIAL (... WHERE state='active'). PostgreSQL supports
      partial indexes; it is gated with a dbms=postgresql precondition (onFail=MARK_RAN) so
      it applies only on Postgres. Elsewhere the at-most-one-active-radio-per-(device,
      radio_id) invariant is enforced by the service (findActive-before-insert), exactly as
      085 does — an idempotent attach resolves an existing active row rather than writing a
      duplicate.
    -->
    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-active-radio-unique" author="hugmesh">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN" onError="MARK_RAN">
            <dbms type="postgresql"/>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>Partial UNIQUE: at most one ACTIVE radio per (device_id, radio_id).
                 Detached rows are excluded so the same radio_id can be re-attached after
                 detach (the audit trail holds the cycles).</comment>
        <sql>
            CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_node_radio_device_active_radio
                ON node_radio_device (device_id, radio_id)
                WHERE state = 'active'
        </sql>
        <rollback>DROP INDEX uq_node_radio_device_active_radio</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-domain-index" author="hugmesh">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN" onError="MARK_RAN">
            <dbms type="postgresql"/>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>Index the per-tenant residency read predicate on node_radio_device.</comment>
        <sql>CREATE INDEX idx_node_radio_device_domain ON node_radio_device (domain)</sql>
        <rollback>DROP INDEX idx_node_radio_device_domain</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-device-index" author="hugmesh">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN" onError="MARK_RAN">
            <dbms type="postgresql"/>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>Index the per-node export scan (the node's active radios).</comment>
        <sql>CREATE INDEX idx_node_radio_device_device ON node_radio_device (device_id)</sql>
        <rollback>DROP INDEX idx_node_radio_device_device</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="300-node-radio-device-grant" author="hugmesh">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN" onError="MARK_RAN">
            <dbms type="postgresql"/>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>GRANT SELECT,INSERT,UPDATE on node_radio_device to the admin_bff role
                 (detach is a CAS UPDATE — the row is never DELETEd = the audit trail).</comment>
        <sql>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON node_radio_device TO admin_bff</sql>
        <rollback>REVOKE SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON node_radio_device FROM admin_bff</rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
